{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Dressing the Part"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Doing Well?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect Tense - Talking About Experiences"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about experience.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span>, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now."}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is common to hear and use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Tense</span> in interviews, since you talk about things you did in the past that connect to the present job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I'<span class=\"strong\">ve worked</span> with close-knit teams.<br></span>= I worked with close-knit teams in the past and now I am familiar with that style of work."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'<span class=\"strong\">ve worked</span> with close-knit teams. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'<span class=\"strong\">ve also had</span> the chance to develop relationships with a diverse range of clients. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "This <span class=\"strong\">has provided</span> me with what I believe to be a solid foundation for this position. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'<span class=\"strong\">ve worked</span> at the University newspaper and the local Boston Review, both with a group and independently."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'<span class=\"strong\">ve taken</span> many courses to help me perform well in this position. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Small Talk"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use small talk (a casual form of conversation) to \"break the ice\" or fill an awkward silence between people. It is common to use small talk at work when you talk to coworkers and when you meet someone new."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are certain \"safe\" topics that people usually make small talk about. Talking about the weather is a common small talk topic. Another one is the traffic or local news. For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Interviewer</span>: You must be Adam.  <br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Hi, Mr. Mitchell. Pleasure to meet you.  <br><span class=\"strong\">Interviewer</span>: Likewise. How are you? <br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I'm good thanks. Yourself?  <br><span class=\"strong\">Interviewer</span>: Not bad. How was your trip? Was the traffic OK?  <br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Yes, everything was fine, thanks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is a typical small talk conversation between two people who do not know each other. It creates a comfortable, friendly atmosphere."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "solid foundation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "good basis of experience and education in preparation for a job"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This experience has provided me with a solid foundation for this position."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about work experience."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "benefits"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "extra advantages of working at a company, such as healthcare and dental insurance"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Are you more interested in a steady job with benefits and holiday entitlement or one that will allow you to advance quickly?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "glass ceiling"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the feeling that you cannot advance in a company, even though it appears you can"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't want to hit a glass ceiling. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "corporate ladder"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the hierarchy in a company that describes who is in charge of who"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to grow and move up the corporate ladder."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "salary requirements"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the amount of money you expect to earn in a job"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What are your annual salary requirements?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le13ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of a dream job. "}, {"type": "text"